cat > README << 'EOF'
# CSE323 Project — xv6 Lottery Scheduler

A lottery-based CPU scheduler for xv6, implemented as a course project
for CSE323.

## Group members
- Sajidul Abedin
- Saif Mahmood Chowdhury
- Kazi Shahriar Sharif

## Project overview
This implements a proportional-share lottery scheduler in xv6, replacing
the default round-robin scheduler. Each process holds a number of
"tickets"; each scheduling decision draws a random ticket and runs
whichever process holds it, so a process with more tickets gets a
proportionally larger share of the CPU.

## Status
- [x] Phase 1 — Process introspection: `pstat.h` / `getpinfo()` syscall,
      extended with CPU burst length, total CPU time, memory size,
      parent PID, and child count. Validated with `ps` and a dedicated
      edge-case harness (`validate.c`).
- [x] Phase 2 — Lottery scheduler: `settickets()`, ticket inheritance on
      `fork()`, randomized proportional scheduling, ticket transfer, and
      ticket exchange. Validated with `lottotest.c` (3:2:1 ratio,
      converges to within ~3% of the theoretical split, with a
      human-readable bar-chart summary printed after every run),
      `transfertest.c`, `exchangetest.c`, and a 16/16-passing edge-case
      suite (`edgetest.c`) covering invalid input, nonexistent PIDs, and
      exact ticket-count boundaries.

## Build & run
    make
    make qemu-nox

Exit QEMU with Ctrl-a then x.

## Validation programs
| Program | What it checks |
|---|---|
| `ps` | Prints live process stats via `getpinfo()` |
| `validate` | NULL-pointer safety, `nchildren`, CPU-time tracking, memory growth via `sbrk` |
| `lottotest` | 3:2:1 ticket ratio converges correctly over time; prints CSV + ASCII bar summary |
| `transfertest` | `transfertickets()` moves the exact requested amount |
| `exchangetest` | `exchangetickets()` performs a full swap |
| `edgetest` | Invalid input, nonexistent PIDs, and exact ticket-count boundaries for every syscall |

## New syscalls
| Syscall | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `getpinfo(struct pstat*)` | Returns PID, PPID, ticket count, ticks, CPU-access count, last burst length, child count, and memory size for every process |
| `settickets(int)` | Sets the calling process's ticket count (fails on input < 1) |
| `transfertickets(int pid, int n)` | Transfers n tickets from caller to pid (fails if it would drop the caller below 1 ticket, or pid doesn't exist) |
| `exchangetickets(int pid)` | Swaps ticket counts between caller and pid |

---

This project is built on [xv6](https://github.com/mit-pdos/xv6-public),
a teaching operating system from MIT, created by Frans Kaashoek, Robert
Morris, and Russ Cox, and inspired by the original Unix v6 by Dennis
Ritchie and Ken Thompson. See the original project for full
acknowledgments and license details.
EOF
